  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_410cfda101464bfea4d622a3fbba4d3d",
      "statement": "The SSSS reference implementation is layered (spec → registry/schemas → frontmatter → validator → kernel → adapters → runtime/semantic/bundle → CLI/transports), and src/kernel.mjs is the sole mutation authority: createKernel() takes injectable adapters (VFS, event store, idempotency store, lease store, authorizer, projection coordinator, resource coordinator) and exposes execute() and recover(), owning the §6.3 stage ordering and semantics while adapters implement mechanics only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ssss-spec.md#L1019-L1023",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4102c20a136cf76cebcfe88517bc10c726c8e30aaad0fb77094bbe77e02ad244:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kernel.mjs#L181-L232",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8739d1afd6f66ed5c5265f1679f44d00896b8134711ff9d278429215b5f374a9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kernel.mjs#L87-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b6bfac65e894832444e6d8d955e4076b1c20445384cba1e8361ef7951cada24b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84af564b523c47e7be1485bf8e5cc4cf",
      "statement": "src/engine.mjs is a thin compatibility façade over the kernel with no second mutation implementation: createEngine() builds a createKernel() per (vaultRoot, eventLogDir) pair and forwards every envelope to kernel.execute(); its only added behavior is legacy principal translation from roles/<role>/ROLE.md permissions into 0.9 capabilities and stripping the ssss: qualifier from the validation type.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/engine.mjs#L1-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:85803fb0ccea2faef73f20a7682f4d1370c4bfb21ad9679b93e2af0ae94ad0c1:"
        },
        {
