          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc2b68e84f300ba6e0fbddd4fd0625a05c37187c4afe8224cd5b0fc97b8fea1c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5861da65629e485e8c07f483aa986c10",
      "statement": "Type validation is registry-driven rather than per-type code: a primitive's required_fields, append_only flag, immutable_fields, references, and portability class all come from registry/core.json plus extensions, so src/validator.mjs and src/registry.mjs validate any primitive (workflow, assistant, or a host extension) by resolving the declared type against the registry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/registry.mjs#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b146a11bf0770daae7ddabe0067d995046f45852b18845485fd4158cf4794fda:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/validator.mjs#L32-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be592e8275efadb32ecac06c4001dcc0398265a118c3399f11044e866033b5d0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ff9a81aa975a4eed91fc86556815ba99",
      "statement": "A mutation flows through the §6.3 pipeline in kernel.execute as one of four envelope types (operation, patch, event, delete), authenticating the principal before any storage read, enforcing idempotency against both the idempotency store and the event log, validating content and append-only/type-immutability rules, authorizing, leasing, and committing; the canonical event append at stage 10 is the commit point before which any failure leaves no trace and after which nothing rolls back, with resource finalize, projections, and idempotency recording (stages 11-13) failing forward as warnings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ssss-spec.md#L1025-L1044",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:adafd591bc30b1c196950623932c5ca0a0b738c031304912de92b39d24040681:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kernel.mjs#L181-L232",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8739d1afd6f66ed5c5265f1679f44d00896b8134711ff9d278429215b5f374a9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kernel.mjs#L414-L522",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7dbd0220d6ae286c2c8fc815bf546f8b7e850be2c92315a333606a98c1b17025:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_50d4b52c3d3942cfaecd195f6b3939a2",
      "statement": "For non-event envelopes the kernel durably records a commit intent (prior content, intended digest, expected event_id) before the stage-9 VFS write and holds the path's commit lock until stage 10 ends; if the writer dies between stages 9 and 10, recover() (run once per kernel before its first operation and before the next commit on the path) resolves the intent from the event log and vault as committed, rolled_back, discarded, or conflict, and a live writer's intent is never touched.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ssss-spec.md#L1046-L1068",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3fe6a208e900942acba237320284bfd81385f03a6106f96b2140e5944f741189:"
